+`HolderStack`, `NeckBands` in `sim::verify::body_bands`, and the three
+app call sites (`operation::job`/`generate`, `fixture_struck`,
+`sim_tool_body`).

From 50992dbaaf7f4ab52b311129e5a08bfbcc8bdce2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:00:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix(sim): drill reach, cross drill and probe stylus read
 the body's band stack

The three laws #835 left on the cylinder enclosing a modelled tool body
now read the band stack the simulation draws: the axial holder-face law
and cross_holder check each band's face disc / swept footprint against
the material over that band's radius, cross_part::part_clear takes the
body-carrying cutter, and probe_op::stylus_cutter is rebuilt as stem +
probe body + the body's bands. A stepped body whose flange never reaches
the material is no longer refused; one whose flange does is, naming the
band. No body (or a stack that does not fit) reads the holder cylinder
bit-identically; the enclosure wording stays only for that fallback.

Stacked on #957 (issue #852).

Fixes #842

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
